                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ed3b53cf-0c93-4c01-b88b-fa52ab71f940",
                        "source_entry_id": "1439e2bc-9cee-313c-bf35-0e9fbdce1d58",
                        "source_sense_id": "a3bdfcda-75f0-3457-b9d7-d30de9057733",
                        "target_lang_word": "Sunni",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Sunni",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bdaf75ff-4b28-395c-a895-d225486b56e5",
                                        "entry_id": "befe8967-0493-332b-8534-3112b3975e93",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Belonging or relating to the branch of Islam based on the Qur'an, the Kutub al-Sittah (the hadiths which record the Sunnah) and that places emphasis on the Sahabah."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c15f9196-1000-4cda-b679-f56ba06e46c7",
                                                "sense_id": "bdaf75ff-4b28-395c-a895-d225486b56e5",
                                                "text": "I therefore strongly advocate the formation of a local capital but not at Hillah, which is too Sunni and near Baghdad"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4df38d42-3bf1-46a6-8e3a-c9c85d82d58e",
                                                "sense_id": "bdaf75ff-4b28-395c-a895-d225486b56e5",
                                                "text": "members […] came to view themselves collectively as the righteous descendants of Husayn confronting an evil and fundamentally alien ruler: a shah more Zoroastrian than Muslim, more Sunni than Shi'i, more Arab than Iranian, more Yazid than Husayn."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "486562ec-693e-4b3d-bc93-68648f56d54f",
                                                "sense_id": "bdaf75ff-4b28-395c-a895-d225486b56e5",
                                                "text": "Many Shias who had become more Sunni in their religious practices reverted back to their original sect."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Sunni",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "87791edc-1fc2-315c-894e-14329d5928d2",
                                        "entry_id": "2b77f935-e819-3c87-b880-e190bacb1ca1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A follower of Sunni Islam."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Sunni",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "68c9cdb0-b705-3bd7-a90a-8b1c8cf883a2",
                                        "entry_id": "71c355e9-fa4f-3f05-a846-48236be9c9d9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Ellipsis of Sunni Islam."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77d65aed-0bfe-45ce-9d93-7a5d94a880f7",
                                                "sense_id": "68c9cdb0-b705-3bd7-a90a-8b1c8cf883a2",
                                                "text": "In Islam, Sunni is a more triumphant version of the faith than Shia, which stresses the importance of suffering, following the founder Ali, who was persecuted."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a695b24-7e41-4b75-814d-4642ca419248",
                                                "sense_id": "68c9cdb0-b705-3bd7-a90a-8b1c8cf883a2",
                                                "text": "Sunni has four schools of Islamic doctrine and law — Hanafi, Maliki, Shafi'i, and Hanbali — which uniquely interpret the Hadith, or recorded oral traditions of Muhammad."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b9a2eb2-7d71-4bd6-8a1c-bf66930a6b38",
                                                "sense_id": "68c9cdb0-b705-3bd7-a90a-8b1c8cf883a2",
                                                "text": "Sunni is the mainstream religion, based in Mecca, and is generally more moderate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ac2db4e9-41fd-4bea-b539-4d14520981b5",
                        "source_entry_id": "1439e2bc-9cee-313c-bf35-0e9fbdce1d58",
                        "source_sense_id": "a3bdfcda-75f0-3457-b9d7-d30de9057733",
                        "target_lang_word": "sunnite",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sunnite",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bb316fa3-1bf4-328b-9cd0-bd3cfd26749a",
                                        "entry_id": "882dafb3-0c6f-358a-81a3-e6ae518fa091",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Qualifie une forme de l'islam orthodoxe et traditionnel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Sunnisme"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "703cd362-be58-4abc-88e4-eb6341e8e096",
                                                "sense_id": "bb316fa3-1bf4-328b-9cd0-bd3cfd26749a",
                                                "text": "La féodalité uzbek (les chefs tribaux, les H’ôzà, traditionnels pourvoyeurs de l'administration, le haut clergé sunnite) voyait avec dépit le pouvoir lui échapper."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "sunnite",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a7cf72e-2ef4-318b-a71e-3ea1a90be561",
                                        "entry_id": "01fc8a7d-d6c2-3b95-853b-51910d268380",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Musulman orthodoxe et qui s’attache à la tradition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Sunnisme"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e8951616-925f-42d1-a5ee-41c613882ee8",
                                                "sense_id": "0a7cf72e-2ef4-318b-a71e-3ea1a90be561",
                                                "text": "— Pour vous, les sunnites, il n’y a effectivement pas de preuve. Vous pensez que Mohammed est mort sans désigner d’héritier, qu’il a laissé les musulmans à l’abandon et qu’alors ils se sont laissé gouverner par le plus fort ou le plus rusé."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8cb449fb-5bd6-473d-84a9-f9f7c9b23d72",
                                                "sense_id": "0a7cf72e-2ef4-318b-a71e-3ea1a90be561",
                                                "text": "Si j'ai tant insisté sur les inconséquences de la politique américaine en Irak depuis 1990, c'est qu'elles ont créé les conditions d'une guerre de religion entre chiites et sunnites, dont nous ne pouvons aujourd'hui prévoir l'issue, sinon qu'elle aura d'immenses répercutions […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c139f3a2-fdf6-4a30-8292-86b4a10da037",
                                                "sense_id": "0a7cf72e-2ef4-318b-a71e-3ea1a90be561",
                                                "text": "Nous proposons un classement des toponymes beyrouthins selon la confession du commémoré ou de l’établissement toponymisé ou le nom de famille, regroupés selon leur classement officiel au Parlement libanais: sunnites, chiites, druzes, alaouites, maronites, grecs-catholiques, grecs-orthodoxes, arméniens orthodoxes et catholiques, minorités chrétiennes, et juifs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5db0706e-a766-4591-a8e4-2f909d06e37f",
                                                "sense_id": "0a7cf72e-2ef4-318b-a71e-3ea1a90be561",
                                                "text": "Après leur rupture avec les sunnites, les musulmans chiites se trouvent en minorité dans l'islam."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fa1af0e0-39b2-4570-b7de-d4c5b24620e7",
                        "source_entry_id": "1439e2bc-9cee-313c-bf35-0e9fbdce1d58",
